  "source_semantics": [
    {
      "area": "Original producer and source",
      "finding": "Opt-in --capture-pair-context only. root must resolve to the running gate ROOT; all GIT overrides rejected; clean git_source required for capture; original source_inputs and actual tools/deps verified before/after by existing gate. Producer changes remain separate from dirty live verifier identity.",
      "preserved_old_functions": [
        "section",
        "bytes_at",
        "contained",
        "validate_pair",
        "imported_gateways",
        "source_inputs",
        "compile_profile"
      ]
    },
    {
      "area": "Before-witness",
      "finding": "Before configure/build, actual M33/Thumb/soft GCC queries select libgcc.a/libc_nano.a/libnosys.a. Original absolute response/raw streams retained. Symlink components and aliased choices rejected; exact bounded bytes/mode plus uid/gid/device/inode/mtime/ctime are sampled and full three-library copies retained. Seven tool identities are likewise locked."
    },
    {
      "area": "After-witness and race window",
      "finding": "Original and retained before library bytes/metadata are checked after build. Every finally selected original library row is again exactly compared with the complete after row while final inventory is built. Report identities cannot be overwritten by a LOAD include. Tools must match both original snapshots and report. The real window-regression tests now detect afterA\u2192inventoryB."
    },
    {
      "area": "Actual FileAPI graph",
      "finding": "Fresh codemodel-v2 query is issued before each normal stage configure. Only the actual u575_secure/u575_nonsecure executable and dependency-reachable STATIC_LIBRARY artifacts authorize local archives; actual emitted DB outputs and exact Secure import provide the remaining local set. Target identity/image/stage, one configuration/index, safe reply names/artifacts, no duplicate IDs/reply filenames/deps, cycles/depth/count and exact visited reply set are checked. Unknown local.a and unknown external LOAD fail; no second library registry."
    },
    {
      "area": "Typed offline recomputation",
      "finding": "Both captured stages must carry typed FileAPI sets. Offline build_pair re-derives the same graph, emitted-output/import/map union, exact source/report/tool/bundle/history identities, and three before/after library SHA/size/mode relationships using retained data only. Absolute historical labels are normalized inert keys, not opened or executed on the receiver."
    },
    {
      "area": "Report/context publication",
      "finding": "Existing report is written once on success before context construction. Context is published last only after build_pair validates its report/history. Successful capture does not rewrite the anchored report. Failed capture produces no successful context and actual failed diagnostics remain; partial outputs are not marked passed."
    },
    {
      "area": "Portable transport and limits",
      "finding": "Externally pinned complete context and outer manifest SHA are required. Strict typed exact role/member union, integer-not-bool schemas, empty raw streams, canonical IDs,128MiB compressed/logical,160MiB expanded,8MiB metadata and4096-entry caps remain. Raw TAR inspection precedes tarfile extensions/materialization, forbids links/sparse/extensions, enforces two zero end blocks/zero-only tail, and single gzip CRC/ISIZE/trailer; metadata reads/cache checked before allocation. Ordinary dotdot cannot place seal output inside source or inputs."
    },
    {
      "area": "Receiver execution",
      "finding": "Only explicitly hash-pinned current nm and objdump may inspect temporary data copies; their bytes must equal original report tool SHA and remain stable afterward. Archived compiler/scripts/argv are data. ELF boundary, SG imports, actual blxns and per-NS-function forbidden privileged instruction checks are recomputed. Current verifier source is independently observed; it is not relabeled as original build source."
    },
    {
      "area": "CI integration",
      "finding": "Exactly one original paired build, now with capture flag, followed by full existing19 real-gate test discovery when CI actually runs. Shell uses quoted run/attempt RUNNER_TEMP outside source, computes explicit context/outer manifest anchors and trusted reader hashes, seal then verify with explicit relocated archive, and copies only opaque transport+manifest after verify success. A fixture executes the actual extracted shell against external stand-ins and proves verify failure31 prevents copied verified-artifact publication. This fixture is not real ARM evidence."
    },
    {
      "area": "Identity/upload and existing consumers",
      "finding": "Original pair raw/context and new opaque evidence root are added to existing always identity/upload only. Old H743 explicit project paths and canonical SPI assemblies remain via preservation of all54 prior workflow method bodies. Single-ELF candidate acceptance and generic store/common implementation are byte-equal HEAD, unchanged; no pair fallback or release-policy weakening."
    }
  ],
